{"node":{"id":"HP:0002151","label":"Increased circulating lactate concentration","ic":3.913,"definition":"Abnormally increased level of blood lactate (2-hydroxypropanoic acid). Lactate is produced from pyruvate by lactate dehydrogenase during normal metabolism. The terms lactate and lactic acid are often used interchangeably but lactate (the component measured in blood) is strictly a weak base whereas lactic acid is the corresponding acid. Lactic acidosis is often used clinically to describe elevated lactate but should be reserved for cases where there is a corresponding acidosis (pH below 7.35)."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0014464","label":"progressive encephalopathy with leukodystrophy due to DECR deficiency","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_9bce2774c765","source":"MONDO:0014464","target":"HP:0002151","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:616034 · PMID:24847004;PMID:27940755","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24847004;PMID:27940755/","level":"observed","date":"2023-02-19","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"2,4-dienoyl-CoA reductase deficiency: Increased circulating lactate concentration (frequency 2/2) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0013971","label":"leukoencephalopathy-thalamus and brainstem anomalies-high lactate syndrome","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_6600642c9374","source":"MONDO:0013971","target":"HP:0002151","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:614924 · OMIM:614924","url":"https://omim.org/entry/614924","level":"curated","date":"2012-11-20","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Combined oxidative phosphorylation deficiency 12: Increased circulating lactate concentration [TAS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.5,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.5},{"id":"MONDO:0012824","label":"leukodystrophy, hypomyelinating, 4","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_ab9e3e718ab2","source